	Step by step Webdriver- Architecture Explanation

 	1. How selenium werb-driver works
       test scripts execution - we write a test scripts using a selenium client(java, python, etc.) in your choosen langugage 

    2. Command translations - The client library translate out test script into json format 
       ( protocal) w3c or json wired 

    3. HTTPS communication : These JSON commands sends over HTTP to the appropriate 	
        browser    driver (CD,FD, SD, OD, ED).

    4. Driver - Browser interactions: The browser driver recivies the command from protocol 
       to perform the specified action (click, dropdown, get, enter)

    5. Handling response: The browser response is sent back through the driver to the
       client library which then proceed with next steps in the scripts.


       Pre-requiste of selenium webdriver
       1. Operating System - minimum window - 10 | Safari - M2
       2. Any latest browser
       3. Minimum java version - 11 (open cmd and type - java -version)
       4. Any Editor - Eclipse or Intellij.
       5. Selenium jar (Selenium Webdriver or Selenium grid). 

       Configuration of Selenium Webdriver
       1. Create 2 Separate Folder
       		a. Yourname_seleniumWorkspace.
       		b. Selenium Jars

       2. Open Selenium.dev website and download selenium grid o webdriver jars
       3. Launch Eclipse
       4. Switch Workspace --> Select folder  which created in step 1.		
       			File > Switch Workspace > Other > Browse > look for folder > Open
       			 > Launch
       5. Create Project - File > New > Java Project > Automation_Webdriver			 
       6. uncheck Create Module-info java file on New Java Project window.
       7. Click on Finish Button.	

       Steps to configurate Selenium Jars in to Project.
       1. Right click on project > Build Path > Configure Build Path
       2. Click on Libraries 
       3. Click on ClassPath
       4. Click on Add External Jars (2nd Option)
       5. Select the selenium jar (download in step number 2). > Open
       6. Click on Apply and close button	
       7. Validate the selenium jar got added into project
       		open project > look for reference libraries > selenium jars will be presented.


